IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ita-types`

-- Income Tax Act 1947 — PART 4: IS THIS INCOME EXEMPT?
--
-- s 13 (exempt income, with the foreign-income exemptions of s 13(7A)-(9) and
-- short-term employment in s 13(6)-(7)), ss 13A-13X (the exemption regimes),
-- and the First Schedule (exempt bodies).
--
-- Most regimes in ss 13A-13X turn on an approval or a prescription by the
-- Minister or an authorised body, given by regulations or letter; their
-- conditions are the approval's. Those grounds are encoded as: exempt if the
-- approval (or prescription) covers the income — an input. Grounds whose
-- conditions the Act itself states are encoded as rules.
--
-- Source: ../source/ITA1947.txt lines 3457-8328, 34113-34180.

§ `Part 4 — exemptions`

§§ `The grounds of exemption`

DECLARE `Exemption ground` IS ONE OF
    -- s 13(1), conditions in the Act
    `s 13(1)(za) dividend from a company resident in Singapore`
    `s 13(1)(zd) individual's interest on a deposit with an approved bank or licensed finance company`
    `s 13(1)(ze), (zf), (zh), (zi), (zj) individual's specified investment income`
    `s 13(1)(t), (ta) non-resident's interest on a deposit with an approved bank`
    `s 13(1)(w) employment on a Singapore ship substantially outside Singapore`
    `s 13(1)(jd) voluntary medisave contribution for a self-employed individual`
    `s 13(1)(j) CPF sums`
    `s 13(1)(d) gains in an SRS account`
    `s 13(1)(i) death gratuities, consolidated compensation for death or injuries`
    `s 13(1)(zb) employer's childcare subsidy`
    `s 13(1)(e) a First Schedule body`
    `s 13(1)(m), (ma) a trade union or platform work association, not from a trade`
    `s 13(1)(zm) a registered or exempt charity`
    `s 13(1) another paragraph whose conditions are met`        -- (a)-(c), (f), (h), (ja), (jb), (k), (l), (oa), (q)-(rb), (v), (x), (y), (zf)-(zy)
    -- s 13(6)-(10)
    `s 13(6) short-term employment of a non-resident`
    `s 13(7A) foreign income received by an individual`
    `s 13(8) foreign dividends, branch profits or service income of a resident`
    -- ss 13A-13X
    `s 13W gain on disposing of shares`
    `s 13Q, 13QA a resident beneficiary's share of trust or estate income`
    `an approved or prescribed regime under ss 13A-13V, 13X`

DECLARE `Exemption facts` HAS
    `recipient`                                    IS A `Kind of person`
    `recipient resident in Singapore`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `received through a partnership in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `derived from carrying on a trade, business or profession` IS A BOOLEAN
    `derived or paid on`                          IS A DATE
    `the payer is a company resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN          -- (za)
    `the recipient has a business or PE in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN       -- (t)
    `days employment exercised in Singapore`      IS A NUMBER            -- s 13(6)
    `as a director of a company`                  IS A BOOLEAN           -- s 13(7)(a)
    `as a public entertainer not substantially supported from foreign public funds` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 13(7)(b)
    `subject to tax in the territory it comes from` IS A BOOLEAN         -- s 13(9)(a), (9A)
    `that territory's headline corporate rate`    IS A NUMBER            -- s 13(9)(b)
    `the Comptroller is satisfied the exemption is beneficial` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 13(7A)(b), (9)(c)
    `the s 13(9)(a) condition waived`             IS A BOOLEAN           -- s 13(9B)
    `on a Singapore ship, exercised substantially outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (w)
    `amount of the income`                        IS A NUMBER
    `an approval or prescription covers the income` IS A BOOLEAN         -- the regimes
    `the conditions of the paragraph are met`     IS A BOOLEAN           -- the other s 13(1) paragraphs
    `the beneficiary's share would be exempt if received directly` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 13Q, 13QA

§§ `The rules`

-- s 13(1)(za): "any dividends paid on or after 1 January 2008 by any company
-- resident in Singapore".
-- (zd): interest derived on or after 1 January 2005 by any individual from a
-- deposit with an approved bank or licensed finance company.
-- (ze), (zf), (zh), (zi), (zj)(i): an individual's interest from debt
-- securities, annuities (not employer- or SRS-bought), life policies, unit
-- trust and REIT distributions, Islamic debt securities, structured products,
-- "except where such income is derived through a partnership in Singapore or
-- is derived from the carrying on of a trade, business or profession".
-- (t): deposit interest of a non-resident individual, or of a non-individual
-- without a business or PE in Singapore ((ta): with a PE, if the funds are
-- not from it — an input as `the conditions … are met`).
-- (w): "employment exercised on board a Singapore ship ... if the employment is
-- exercised substantially outside Singapore".
-- (jd): a voluntary medisave contribution for a self-employed individual, "up
-- to ... (ii) $2,730 per year (for contributions made in 2018 and ... each
-- subsequent year)", less earlier contributions as employer.
-- s 13(6): employment "exercised in Singapore for not more than 60 days in the
-- year preceding any year of assessment by a person who is not resident in
-- Singapore", (7) not a director's emoluments nor a public entertainer's
-- (unless substantially supported from foreign public funds).
-- s 13(7A): foreign income received in Singapore "(a) by any individual who is
-- not resident in Singapore; and (b) on or after 1 January 2004 by any
-- individual who is resident in Singapore if the Comptroller is satisfied that
-- the tax exemption would be beneficial ..., but excludes such income received
-- ... through a partnership in Singapore."
-- s 13(8), (9): foreign dividends, branch profits and service income received
-- by a resident (not an individual, or an individual through a partnership),
-- if "(a) the income is subject to tax of a similar character ... (b) ... the
-- highest rate of tax ... on any gains or profits from any trade or business
-- carried on by any company in that territory ... is not less than 15%; and
-- (c) the Comptroller is satisfied that the tax exemption would be beneficial";
-- (9B) (a) may be waived.
@ref s 13(1), (6), (7), (7A), (8), (9), (9B); ss 13Q, 13QA; First Schedule
GIVEN g IS AN `Exemption ground`
      f IS AN `Exemption facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the income is exempt under` g `:` f IF
    CONSIDER g
    WHEN `s 13(1)(za) dividend from a company resident in Singapore` THEN
            f's `the payer is a company resident in Singapore`
        AND f's `derived or paid on` AT LEAST YMD 2008 1 1
    WHEN `s 13(1)(zd) individual's interest on a deposit with an approved bank or licensed finance company` THEN
            `an individual`
        AND f's `derived or paid on` AT LEAST YMD 2005 1 1
    WHEN `s 13(1)(ze), (zf), (zh), (zi), (zj) individual's specified investment income` THEN
            `an individual`
        AND NOT f's `received through a partnership in Singapore`
        AND NOT f's `derived from carrying on a trade, business or profession`
    WHEN `s 13(1)(t), (ta) non-resident's interest on a deposit with an approved bank` THEN
            NOT f's `recipient resident in Singapore`
        AND (`an individual` OR (NOT f's `the recipient has a business or PE in Singapore`) OR f's `the conditions of the paragraph are met`)
    WHEN `s 13(1)(w) employment on a Singapore ship substantially outside Singapore` THEN
        f's `on a Singapore ship, exercised substantially outside Singapore`
    WHEN `s 13(1)(jd) voluntary medisave contribution for a self-employed individual` THEN
        f's `amount of the income` GREATER THAN 0      -- exempt "up to" $2,730: see `the exempt part of a voluntary medisave contribution of`
    WHEN `s 13(1)(j) CPF sums` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 13(1)(d) gains in an SRS account` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 13(1)(i) death gratuities, consolidated compensation for death or injuries` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 13(1)(zb) employer's childcare subsidy` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 13(1)(e) a First Schedule body` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 13(1)(m), (ma) a trade union or platform work association, not from a trade` THEN
        NOT f's `derived from carrying on a trade, business or profession`
    WHEN `s 13(1)(zm) a registered or exempt charity` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 13(1) another paragraph whose conditions are met` THEN f's `the conditions of the paragraph are met`
    WHEN `s 13(6) short-term employment of a non-resident` THEN
            NOT f's `recipient resident in Singapore`
        AND f's `days employment exercised in Singapore` AT MOST 60
        AND NOT "(7)(a)" ... f's `as a director of a company`
        AND NOT "(7)(b)" ... f's `as a public entertainer not substantially supported from foreign public funds`
    WHEN `s 13(7A) foreign income received by an individual` THEN
            `an individual`
        AND (    "(a)" ... NOT f's `recipient resident in Singapore`
             OR  "(b)" ... (    f's `derived or paid on` AT LEAST YMD 2004 1 1
                            AND f's `the Comptroller is satisfied the exemption is beneficial`
                            AND NOT f's `received through a partnership in Singapore`))
    WHEN `s 13(8) foreign dividends, branch profits or service income of a resident` THEN
            f's `recipient resident in Singapore`
        AND (    "(d)" ... ((NOT `an individual`) AND f's `derived or paid on` AT LEAST YMD 2003 6 1)
             OR  "(f)" ... (`an individual` AND f's `received through a partnership in Singapore` AND f's `derived or paid on` AT LEAST YMD 2004 1 1))
        AND "(9)(a)" ... (f's `subject to tax in the territory it comes from` OR f's `the s 13(9)(a) condition waived`)
        AND "(9)(b)" ... f's `that territory's headline corporate rate` AT LEAST 15%
        AND "(9)(c)" ... f's `the Comptroller is satisfied the exemption is beneficial`
    WHEN `s 13W gain on disposing of shares` THEN f's `the conditions of the paragraph are met`   -- see `the share disposal gain is exempt …`
    WHEN `s 13Q, 13QA a resident beneficiary's share of trust or estate income` THEN
        f's `recipient resident in Singapore` AND f's `the beneficiary's share would be exempt if received directly`
    WHEN `an approved or prescribed regime under ss 13A-13V, 13X` THEN f's `an approval or prescription covers the income`
    WHERE
        `an individual` MEANS f's `recipient` EQUALS `an individual`

§§ `Disposal of shares (s 13W)`

-- s 13W(1): a company's gains on disposing of ordinary shares "(a) during the
-- period between 1 June 2012 to 31 December 2025 ...; and (b) after [it] has,
-- at all times during a continuous period of at least 24 months ending on the
-- date immediately prior to the date of disposal ..., legally and beneficially
-- owned at least 20% of the ordinary shares". (1A): from 1 January 2026,
-- ordinary or preference shares, with at least 20% of the ordinary shares or
-- of the paid-up ordinary and preference share capital by value. (1B): from
-- 1 January 2026, the 20% may be held with group companies (more than 50%
-- links, (1C)) at the start of the 24 months, the subject shares themselves held
-- for 24 months.
-- The exclusions in s 13W(3) onwards (unlisted property companies, insurers,
-- partnerships, and the like) are an input.
DECLARE `Share disposal` HAS
    `disposed on`                                      IS A DATE
    `ordinary shares only`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `months the 20% holding was held continuously before disposal` IS A NUMBER
    `the 20% counts group companies' holdings`         IS A BOOLEAN   -- (1B)
    `the subject shares held for at least 24 months`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (1B)(b)
    `an exclusion in s 13W(3) onwards applies`         IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 13W(1), (1A), (1B)
GIVEN d IS A `Share disposal`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the share disposal gain is exempt under s 13W:` d IF
        NOT d's `an exclusion in s 13W(3) onwards applies`
    AND d's `months the 20% holding was held continuously before disposal` AT LEAST 24
    AND (    "(1)"  ... (d's `ordinary shares only` AND (NOT d's `the 20% counts group companies' holdings`) AND d's `disposed on` AT LEAST YMD 2012 6 1 AND d's `disposed on` AT MOST YMD 2025 12 31)
         OR  "(1A)" ... ((NOT d's `the 20% counts group companies' holdings`) AND d's `disposed on` AT LEAST YMD 2026 1 1)
         OR  "(1B)" ... (d's `the 20% counts group companies' holdings` AND d's `the subject shares held for at least 24 months` AND d's `disposed on` AT LEAST YMD 2026 1 1))

§§ `The First Schedule`

@ref First Schedule Parts A, B
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the First Schedule bodies` MEANS
    LIST "Bankruptcy Estates Account", "Central Co-operative Fund", "Central Sikh Gurdwara Board", "Common Fund",
         "Dependants' Protection Insurance Fund", "Education Finance Board", "Hindu Endowments Board", "Home Protection Fund",
         "Hotels Licensing Board", "Institute of Technical Education, Singapore", "Land Surveyors Board",
         "Majlis Ugama Islam, Singapura", "MediShield Life Fund", "Minister for Finance", "National Arts Council",
         "National Council of Social Service", "National Heritage Board", "National Library Board", "People's Association",
         "Science Centre Board", "Singapore Academy of Law", "Singapore Corporation of Rehabilitative Enterprises",
         "Catholic Young Men's Association", "Lee Kuan Yew Exchange Fellowship", "Metropolitan Young Men's Christian Association",
         "National Crime Prevention Council of Singapore", "SAFRA National Service Association", "HomeTeamNS",
         "Titular Anglican Bishop of Singapore", "Titular Roman Catholic Archbishop of Singapore",
         "Young Men's Christian Association", "Young Women's Christian Association"

-- Part A item 23: "Any specified statutory corporation within the meaning of
-- section 3 of the Statutory Corporations (Contributions to Consolidated Fund)
-- Act 1989" — an input.
@ref s 13(1)(e); First Schedule
GIVEN body IS A STRING
      `a specified statutory corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a First Schedule body:` body `, specified statutory corporation:` `a specified statutory corporation` IF
    elem body `the First Schedule bodies` OR `a specified statutory corporation`

§§ `The exempt amount of a medisave contribution (s 13(1)(jd))`

-- s 13(1)(jd): a voluntary medisave contribution for a self-employed individual
-- is exempt "up to ... (ii) $2,730 per year (for contributions made in 2018 and in
-- each subsequent year), less any previous contribution ... in the person's
-- capacity as an employer". Found by the independent test pass: the exemption
-- reaches the first $2,730, not only contributions of $2,730 or less.
@ref s 13(1)(jd)
GIVEN contribution             IS A NUMBER
      `earlier as an employer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the exempt part of a voluntary medisave contribution of` contribution `, earlier as an employer` `earlier as an employer` MEANS
    IF contribution GREATER THAN `room` THEN `room` ELSE contribution
    WHERE
        `room` MEANS IF `earlier as an employer` GREATER THAN 2730 THEN 0 ELSE 2730 MINUS `earlier as an employer`
